## Final Judgement
The fact-check evidence consistently shows that the World Bank and International Monetary Fund were established at the Bretton Woods Conference in 1944, with key architects being Henry Morgenthau, Harry Dexter White, and John Maynard Keynes. Dr. José Rizal was executed in 1896, nearly five decades before these institutions were created, and Ferdinand Marcos was a young lawyer in 1944 with no documented role in their founding. No verifiable documents or official histories list either individual as a founder or co-founder. The claim is therefore historically false and directly contradicted by all retrieved evidence.

